# Netlify redirects.
#
# Format:  <from-path>  <to-path>  <status>
# One rule per line; add new lines at the bottom. Rules are matched top to
# bottom, first match wins.
#
# Netlify serves these at the CDN edge, before the request reaches Next, so
# they win over next.config.js redirects and over the SSR 404 handler. The
# trailing "!" forces the rule, which is what makes it beat that handler.
#
# Note: these cannot be tested with `npm run dev` - there is no Netlify edge in
# front of it, so the file is simply never read. Use `npx netlify dev`, or
# verify on a deploy.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Old category-path URLs -> /blog/<slug>
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Posts used to live under /creative-experiences-behind-the-image/<slug>. They
# now live under /blog/<slug>, so the old paths 404. These rules point the
# links that are already out in the world (newsletters, search results) at the
# posts' current homes.

# "5 Dragon Women" was also renamed - the piece covers six women - so the slug
# changed as well as the prefix.
/creative-experiences-behind-the-image/5-women-become-a-fire-breathing-dragon  /blog/6-women-become-a-fire-breathing-dragon  301!
/creative-experiences-behind-the-image/6-women-become-a-fire-breathing-dragon  /blog/6-women-become-a-fire-breathing-dragon  301!

/creative-experiences-behind-the-image/our-51st-wedding-anniversary  /blog/our-51st-wedding-anniversary  301!

# Old slug under the current prefix, for anyone who has the renamed post
# bookmarked at its pre-rename slug.
/blog/5-women-become-a-fire-breathing-dragon  /blog/6-women-become-a-fire-breathing-dragon  301!

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Retired page URLs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Both 404 today and appeared in a site audit. /contact-us is the old spelling
# of the contact page; /wall is a truncated form of /wall-art, which already
# redirects to /gallery.
/contact-us  /contact   301!
/wall        /gallery   301!

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Specific rules (must stay ABOVE the wildcards below - first match wins)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# "portriat" is a misspelling that never existed as a post. data/blog-redirects.json
# maps these three old prefixes to /blog/<same-typo-slug>, which 404s - so today
# they are a 301 into a dead end. These rules land on the correctly spelled post
# instead, and being edge rules they run before that next.config.js redirect.
/confidence/chandra-and-the-playful-tiger-a-calgary-portriat-session  /blog/chandra-and-the-playful-tiger-a-calgary-portrait-session  301!
/boudoir/chandra-and-the-playful-tiger-a-calgary-portriat-session     /blog/chandra-and-the-playful-tiger-a-calgary-portrait-session  301!
/blogs/chandra-and-the-playful-tiger-a-calgary-portriat-session       /blog/chandra-and-the-playful-tiger-a-calgary-portrait-session  301!

# The same misspelling under the four category prefixes. The wildcards at the
# bottom would otherwise map these to /blog/<same-typo-slug>, which 404s - a
# 301 into a dead end. Only the creative-experiences one is a URL the post ever
# had (that is its category); the other three are defensive, since the slug is
# the part that is wrong and any prefix could have been crawled.
/planning-your-session/chandra-and-the-playful-tiger-a-calgary-portriat-session          /blog/chandra-and-the-playful-tiger-a-calgary-portrait-session  301!
/creative-experiences-behind-the-image/chandra-and-the-playful-tiger-a-calgary-portriat-session  /blog/chandra-and-the-playful-tiger-a-calgary-portrait-session  301!
/confidence-healing-body-image/chandra-and-the-playful-tiger-a-calgary-portriat-session  /blog/chandra-and-the-playful-tiger-a-calgary-portrait-session  301!
/client-stories/chandra-and-the-playful-tiger-a-calgary-portriat-session                 /blog/chandra-and-the-playful-tiger-a-calgary-portrait-session  301!

# No post has ever used the slug "what-to-wear" - searched every title and slug
# in WordPress and there is no wardrobe/outfit article. The nearest real content
# is an FAQ entry ("Can I bring my own outfits?"). Rather than let the wildcard
# send these to /blog/what-to-wear (a 404), each lands on its own category
# archive, which is topically the closest page that returns 200.
/planning-your-session/what-to-wear                  /blog/planning-your-session                  301!
/creative-experiences-behind-the-image/what-to-wear  /blog/creative-experiences-behind-the-image  301!
/confidence-healing-body-image/what-to-wear          /blog/confidence-healing-body-image          301!
/client-stories/what-to-wear                         /blog/client-stories                         301!

# Legacy URL carrying a literal colon and mixed case in the slug.
/blogs/from-heartbreak-to-healing:-Boudoir-after-Divorce  /blog/from-heartbreak-to-healing-boudoir-after-divorce  301!

# Capitalised variant of /yoga. The lowercase /yoga is a Next page that issues
# its own redirect to the same place; path matching here is case-sensitive, so
# this rule only ever sees the uppercase form and the two do not collide.
/Yoga  https://yoga.innerspiritphoto.com/  301!

# Old blog index slug.
/blog/nude-blog  /blog  301!

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Wildcards (must stay LAST)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every post under these four category prefixes now lives at /blog/<same-slug>;
# verified across all 96 posts that the slug is identical on both sides, so the
# splat maps cleanly. Renamed posts (the dragon above) and the misspelled slug
# are handled by the specific rules earlier in this file, which win.
/planning-your-session/*                  /blog/:splat   301!
/creative-experiences-behind-the-image/*  /blog/:splat   301!
/confidence-healing-body-image/*          /blog/:splat   301!
/client-stories/*                         /blog/:splat   301!
